{
  "schema": "research-public-artifact/v1",
  "concept": "WiredTiger block reuse, file fragmentation and freeStorageSize",
  "slug": "wiredtiger-block-reuse-file-fragmentation-and-freestoragesize",
  "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c6a5a8335ee9cf749f5b6b58a4e875b48348a0615c450a25d192e35c0786c7bc",
  "canonical_artifact_sha256": "7e1ed8c7406481232a9a388c2f00d57f517529aff71586a5efe3b85a740d51b3",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "clm:ef712c0dfa072d2ac0b853740746ec5d773d3bfa4faf315bcc1a384051ea6c79",
      "text": "collStats.freeStorageSize reports storage available for reuse. The scale argument changes its units, and the documented field can be absent when no storage is available for reuse. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/collStats.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:311562b156f1dd8fa2fc86549fd9aa7216349c3779178893f4c311acd1c7c495"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:4b310b9ae002ee092942224cc2f1ff90c9bcbd64c387b198616971589912c1a4",
      "text": "Compaction is best effort: block placement can prevent a file-size reduction even when reusable bytes remain. A successful command response alone does not establish that physical disk space was reclaimed. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://source.wiredtiger.com/develop/arch-compact.html",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/compact.md",
        "https://www.percona.com/blog/using-compact-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-from-version-4-4/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:56db039baa47b15bde978ee7c3a0e9f2d5345ef1cc5fd284846e9e7115a4ebbc",
        "ev:9ad4268be30f0cbd932ea2c2427d3a66fdb8d9dcc71a2bcf88d5f6e66d326ea6",
        "ev:e33b18315640d4b46f7e36705858a25497d54664012e485bdcca029b7e3198d6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:340b3bf2b0e7a44bb51d0fcca75bf1039a1b2dde6555d4449ff86338cea0bdf9",
      "text": "A collection compact operation covers the collection and its associated indexes. Because collection storageSize excludes indexes, that single metric is insufficient to describe the operation's complete storage footprint. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/compact.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/collStats.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:56db039baa47b15bde978ee7c3a0e9f2d5345ef1cc5fd284846e9e7115a4ebbc",
        "ev:72e6a7436da99a532e54dd6a77a63b207daaf5a896fd5e11434c0faaae36ab58",
        "ev:923479c15c19883915720c5c7618fb3d845eae26f35283ea5b4e3f9f76dc8ed2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:8b870098468668e595566362f5e61f7bc3d9d33434e503b5e480fdecc7bd17a0",
      "text": "Dropping a collection or index releases the disk space occupied by that object, unlike deleting individual documents while retaining the object's files. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/faq/storage.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/en/mongodb/use-cases/defragment-a-disk-to-improve-disk-usage"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:a7a23a4cb1b4680117a31ff38ea860e3bde995bdeec439d5a2321ab083f466ea"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:ef3b0c57f8a6a5b332f6ba84985ab38f8e553419e996ea00c51c8aab974c771a",
      "text": "Deleting documents leaves space inside WiredTiger data files available for later reuse; it does not generally return those bytes to the operating system. Logical data reduction therefore need not reduce filesystem usage. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/faq/storage.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/en/mongodb/use-cases/defragment-a-disk-to-improve-disk-usage",
        "https://www.percona.com/blog/using-compact-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-from-version-4-4/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:a7a23a4cb1b4680117a31ff38ea860e3bde995bdeec439d5a2321ab083f466ea"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:6c83612a6391d00c2b576c9cab2936ff2340cb1569afb1e6ebe980a8e60ad586",
      "text": "The wiredTiger.block-manager statistic named \"file bytes available for reuse\" measures internal reusable space in bytes; it is not a measurement of filesystem free capacity. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/faq/storage.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.percona.com/blog/using-compact-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-from-version-4-4/",
        "https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/en/mongodb/use-cases/defragment-a-disk-to-improve-disk-usage"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:38446b619cd2561ae5ba8d8c61bd58eb136c22930257c32186a2c93626ee19a2",
        "ev:a7a23a4cb1b4680117a31ff38ea860e3bde995bdeec439d5a2321ab083f466ea"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:21e50e5b47f511e8565f7772afae65f7710c031eeebb7e0fcd44f99bc258d9bb",
      "text": "storageSize includes allocated collection storage, including unused allocation, and reflects compression; it excludes indexes. totalSize adds totalIndexSize. Comparing logical size directly with storageSize is therefore not a reliable measure of WiredTiger free blocks. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/collStats.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/faq/storage.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:4cc1912b860a1d8a064da6ebec0e3e1210e3a1e8739aad87213c72368790421c",
        "ev:72e6a7436da99a532e54dd6a77a63b207daaf5a896fd5e11434c0faaae36ab58",
        "ev:923479c15c19883915720c5c7618fb3d845eae26f35283ea5b4e3f9f76dc8ed2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:ce421e46c1bda50964cc331ea7e5c202d9c20716125f126eb68d19ccdf873ac9",
      "text": "WiredTiger retains blocks referenced by checkpoints. Replacing a page does not make its previous disk block reusable until the checkpoint referencing that block has been removed and checkpoint metadata has been resolved. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://source.wiredtiger.com/develop/arch-compact.html",
      "also": [
        "https://github.com/wiredtiger/wiredtiger/wiki/Block-Manager-Overview"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:9ad4268be30f0cbd932ea2c2427d3a66fdb8d9dcc71a2bcf88d5f6e66d326ea6",
        "ev:ad05ab9d33ff9bc2eda8388efe0a5d007b226bab11acf48e18e90d701d49df83",
        "ev:ff18a08a1a76836c2e4ca3d431d61cac44e0c41d03638e6359aa2f3da9f59f9a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:6140b4c05a4dae5fdc4ef4cccc5cc450773fa8cbc9eb04be4ba994fd23624b83",
      "text": "Compaction can move live blocks from a file's end into reusable blocks near its beginning, then truncate the free tail. Interior holes are therefore potential relocation destinations, even though truncation itself occurs at the file end. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://source.wiredtiger.com/develop/arch-compact.html",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/compact.md",
        "https://github.com/wiredtiger/wiredtiger/wiki/Block-Manager-Overview"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:9ad4268be30f0cbd932ea2c2427d3a66fdb8d9dcc71a2bcf88d5f6e66d326ea6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:856e9035c7f5a27212d1b066af4f42a2acb5837e82c3455bca76765bde93791b",
      "text": "Measure collection statistics before and after compaction and check filesystem disk usage as well. The collection statistics describe internal allocation; filesystem usage establishes whether space was actually returned. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/compact.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.percona.com/blog/using-compact-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-from-version-4-4/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:255f14287ea6b68d5721d64b469641be61acfc35c84955b47e5d0ccc5647d2ac",
        "ev:56db039baa47b15bde978ee7c3a0e9f2d5345ef1cc5fd284846e9e7115a4ebbc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:42f6fba1b3fb23351125e21a5dde99ee84c999e5248f27e42ec4f47ba2b06f85",
      "text": "A compact operation covers both collection data and its associated indexes. A collection-only reusable-space statistic should not be treated as a complete prediction of the total bytes the operation will free. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/compact.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/collStats.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:56db039baa47b15bde978ee7c3a0e9f2d5345ef1cc5fd284846e9e7115a4ebbc",
        "ev:72e6a7436da99a532e54dd6a77a63b207daaf5a896fd5e11434c0faaae36ab58",
        "ev:923479c15c19883915720c5c7618fb3d845eae26f35283ea5b4e3f9f76dc8ed2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:51b6d34fdaffbdb1dd4d2959576f6afd827921dfc4cf924988224cca7c51b3c9",
      "text": "Percona's published PSMDB 6.0.14 experiment reported 306188288 reusable collection bytes before compaction, 34000896 afterward, and bytesFreed of 507662336 while inserts continued. These observations are a workload-specific example, not a universal conversion from reusable bytes to returned disk space. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.percona.com/blog/using-compact-in-percona-server-for-mongodb-from-version-4-4/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:71737ac37753278967989fc27c1d2364ba4dcd7b889fdcf8713e36c75f11af22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:60b6999e3a51aa7dea384a79cb1483f2d911edc0faffdaea81c8b0e56f07b0dc",
      "text": "collStats.freeStorageSize reports storage available for reuse. Treat it as an internal free-space measure, not a guarantee that compact will return that many bytes to the operating system. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/collStats.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/compact.md",
        "https://source.wiredtiger.com/develop/arch-compact.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:311562b156f1dd8fa2fc86549fd9aa7216349c3779178893f4c311acd1c7c495",
        "ev:56db039baa47b15bde978ee7c3a0e9f2d5345ef1cc5fd284846e9e7115a4ebbc",
        "ev:9ad4268be30f0cbd932ea2c2427d3a66fdb8d9dcc71a2bcf88d5f6e66d326ea6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:aab0c6276b967602f0fcc177dbb24d0ab65e8353886935856cf49f926e2e9c14",
      "text": "For a collection-level internal-free-space ratio, compare freeStorageSize with storageSize using consistent units. This ratio describes internal capacity; it does not describe where free blocks lie or guarantee a reclaimable-byte total. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/en/mongodb/use-cases/defragment-a-disk-to-improve-disk-usage",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/collStats.md",
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/compact.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:56db039baa47b15bde978ee7c3a0e9f2d5345ef1cc5fd284846e9e7115a4ebbc",
        "ev:67367cf52156874fafdba1397bab84f9739873a926f89856e61012b46f24fdd0",
        "ev:72e6a7436da99a532e54dd6a77a63b207daaf5a896fd5e11434c0faaae36ab58",
        "ev:8cd42278897495aa33a9ae331ec149dbda57b7c4f9ab8ef4fbb4e8ff2f59f6ec"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:b22c0b8bc4517169ff3b0480eb4b81839f811680b33af77a685de0e186f05a08",
      "text": "The WiredTiger architecture guide warns that its descriptions do not track every code change or necessarily apply to a specific release. Its compaction thresholds should not be presented as a universal MongoDB or Atlas service contract. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://source.wiredtiger.com/develop/arch-compact.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:9ad4268be30f0cbd932ea2c2427d3a66fdb8d9dcc71a2bcf88d5f6e66d326ea6"
      ]
    }
  ],
